Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||06-21-2001||02:43 PM||||Ya I recently broke off my door key in the pasener side lock. So now the paenger door is useless.  <P>My question is would it be better to order a new lock set than to take out the lock and take it to a lock smith?  I am thinking get a whole new set because both locks are/were stubborn and hard to turn and what not.  Has anyone had to do this to thier fiero?<P>thanks in advance for any help,<BR>Dan<P>ps- are the locks one of thoose universal gm parts or are they fiero specific?  Where is the best place to get a new set of locks?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||06-21-2001||02:45 PM||||Mine drivers side is broke.  Damn cheap GM.<P>Fiero Store sells them for 22 bucks.  I heard its a pain to do, I am going to do it when I do the dew (strips)||||reg||14
Z||000002||ROB MAC||06-21-2001||02:55 PM||||See if the inside of the lock ( remove door panel inside ) has a small hole to insert something to push out the key piece. Then squirt the lock full of graphite. If that doesn't work you can proceed with replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan86gt3.8||06-21-2001||11:51 PM||||Ya looks like I will probably get them from fiero store.  They are new right?  I was also thinking that autozone might have them or something.  <P>I have messed with all the locks before so I know its a pain.  I had to mess with all that when I took of my door skins to paint the car.  I know how all the linkage and stuff works.  I was just wondering the best place to get them.  Forgot all about that handy fiero store  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !  <P>thanks,<BR>Dan<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||06-22-2001||12:07 AM|||| I just did the doorlock thing. Got the lock set from the Fiero Store and proceeded to remove the locks via Cadavers method. The first one took a couple of hours because I tied to bullie my way through it. After talking with Cadaver, I finished it in good time. The passenger side took about 45 minutes and most of that was trying to get the little spring clip back on the lock armeture.<BR>refer to my previous post for Cadavers instructions. It should be a few days back. Also, I will need to replace my door moulding trim clips now. Oh well, now my doors work great.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT-maniac||06-22-2001||09:02 PM||||You could get them from the Fiero store but why bother ?. My local dealer just ordered me a set and keyed the locks right there, no problem. Probably cheaper than the fiero store too.||||reg||1
