Z||000007||Adrift||07-02-2001||01:43 AM||||If you have some cash to burn buy yourself a kit car magazine - there are locks advertised in their for the fiero which come with remotes from remote locking / unlocking...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||07-02-2001||10:13 PM||||Fiero Store is 22 bucks.  Local dealer is about 20 bucks I would guess.  <P>Support a.) Local money grubbing dealer who could give a sh!t about your Fiero and its future parts availibilty or b.) Fiero only company with no negative words to be spoken against it who actually cares about your Fiero.<P>Your call.  <P>p.s. I do not work for the Fiero Store and understand they are often times over priced, but a difference of a few bucks is another thing.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||07-03-2001||05:18 AM||||On the other hand, my local dealership loves me.  I went down there yesterday after work just to visit.  They cut me good deals all the time and usually do fabulous work.  They fit me in when I'm in a bind and don't mind when I ask them a million stupid questions.  I'd rather spend my money at my local dealership if it's only a matter of a few bucks difference.  I like dealing with someone face to face.  (disclaimer---my local dealership is probably an exception)<BR><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
